WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:06.930
In the aftermath of the disastrous Exxon Valdez
oil spill of 1989, the SCP Foundation received

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:11.340
a tip about some anomalous plant life surrounding
the affected area.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.740
Plants there were beginning to mutate and
change for seemingly no reason.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.000
With concerns about pollution on everyone’s
mind, it seemed possible that the plant life

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.360
had been directly affected by the oil spill
itself.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.840
After all, humanity’s destructive impact
on the Earth had already become noticeable

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.400
even decades ago.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.920
However, when the Foundation showed up to
investigate, they found something much stranger.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:40.320
All of the mutated plants had a common substance
on them, in their pollen, seeds, roots, or

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.560
the surrounding soil, and we’re not talking
about the millions of gallons of spilled crude

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.560
oil.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:51.420
No one had ever seen this substance before,
and all tests on it proved inconclusive.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:58.050
They collected samples of it and began extensive
studies of what would become known as SCP-1100.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:03.550
Though SCP-1100 was initially classified as
Safe in the Foundation records, it would quickly

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:06.580
reveal itself to be anything but.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.780
The first entry in SCP-1100’s official file
described it as a complex organic substance

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.070
that causes anomalous transformations in natural
plant life.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:19.110
It can be transmitted between plants by way
of pollen and seeds.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:25.430
Within 72 hours, an infected plant becomes
dangerous or hostile to human life.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:31.270
During testing, Foundation researchers exposed
a variety of edible plants to SCP-1100, artificially

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:34.150
pollinating the plants with samples of the
compound.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:39.250
Tomatoes, apples, strawberries, carrots, and
cabbage were among the plants tested.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:44.170
As the fruits and vegetables ripened, many
visual differences became apparent right away.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:48.901
The skin of the tomatoes thickened and darkened
into an off-putting leathery brown until it

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:52.810
was incredibly difficult to bite through or
even slice into with a knife.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:57.920
When the tomatoes were finally cut into pieces,
the flesh was coarse and dry.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.340
The cabbage took on the appearance of rotten
food, growing a fine layer of mold as the

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.770
leaves became slick and oily.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.919
The strawberries sprouted incredibly sharp
thorns where ordinary strawberries simply

00:02:08.919 --> 00:02:12.030
had seeds, becoming unsafe to eat.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:16.900
The carrots and apples were visibly unchanged
but had some unfortunate side effects when

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.580
fed to D-class personnel at the site.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.440
The carrots induced nearly instantaneous vomiting
and dizziness, triggering a seizure in one

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.159
particularly unfortunate subject.

00:02:27.159 --> 00:02:31.389
The apples, on the other hand, had developed
hard, sharp structures near the core.

00:02:31.389 --> 00:02:35.860
Much like the classic urban legend of the
razor blade hidden in the Halloween apple,

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:41.120
personnel who sampled the fruit suffered lacerations
to their gums, tongue, and roof of the mouth.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:46.439
Whether through disgusting appearance, tougher
skin, and thorns, or harmful side effects,

00:02:46.439 --> 00:02:49.529
all of the plants were rendered completely
inedible.

00:02:49.529 --> 00:02:52.599
Initial containment procedures were not terribly
strict.

00:02:52.599 --> 00:02:57.810
SCP-1100 was kept within the Secure Biohazardous
Materials Storage unit at Bio-Containment

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.379
Site 33.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:05.650
This seemed to adequately contain the substance,
until one day during a bit of routine scientific

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:06.650
testing.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:12.129
A large amount of SCP-1100 was gathered for
experimentation, when out of nowhere it vaporized,

00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:13.890
disappearing into the air.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:18.379
Not only did it contaminate the plant life
specifically set aside for the experiment,

00:03:18.379 --> 00:03:23.319
but it traveled through the vents and infected
all of the plant life being grown at the site.

00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:27.909
Specifics of the incident have been redacted
from the record, but 70% of the on-site personnel

00:03:27.909 --> 00:03:30.400
were killed in this containment breach.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:35.980
In the aftermath, the remainder of SCP-1100
was moved to Bio-Containment Site 26.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:40.870
The object’s class, formerly listed as “safe,”
was upgraded to “Euclid.”

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:46.720
After it was transferred to Site 26, experimentation
with SCP-1100 resumed.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.249
After being exposed to the substance, this
new round of plants transformed in a variety

00:03:51.249 --> 00:03:56.329
of ways within 48 hours, with increasingly
disturbing results.

00:03:56.329 --> 00:03:59.549
A mango tree underwent a chemical transformation.

00:03:59.549 --> 00:04:04.079
The fruit, previously ripe and fragrant, became
filled with highly corrosive acid.

00:04:04.079 --> 00:04:08.430
When touched, the transformed mangos would
burst, spraying this caustic liquid all over

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.219
the person who touched them.

00:04:10.219 --> 00:04:14.489
Long vines of common ivy developed muscle-like
internal structures.

00:04:14.489 --> 00:04:19.150
One poor D-Class made the mistake of putting
his hand a bit too close to an infected ivy

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:23.310
plant, only to have it wrap around his hand
and crush the bone into powder before he could

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.310
get away.

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:29.530
A rose bush’s thorns elongated, hardening
and sharpening to a point comparable to a

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:30.530
knife.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:34.910
Another rose bush excreted a toxic substance
from its thorns that, when tested, was found

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:39.230
to be similar to the type of neurotoxin found
in the deadly cone snail.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:44.520
As these experiments continued at Site 26,
several of the researchers assigned to SCP-1100

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:50.400
noted that it was becoming increasingly dangerous
to contain and that its effects were becoming

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:55.000
stronger, more pronounced, and taking effect
much more quickly.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.340
At this point, no source could be found for
the substance, though a theory was posited

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:03.780
by Dr. Smith that it was the creation of a
radical environmentalist group with access

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:07.730
to resources and technology on the same level
as the Foundation.

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:12.660
A task force was put together to monitor environmentalist
groups around the globe for possible hints

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.700
about the creator of SCP-1100.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:21.660
During the course of the experiments at Site
26, SCP-1100 vaporized spontaneously again.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:27.650
It spread throughout the office in record
time, wiping out 96% of the on-site personnel.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:32.030
At that point, in a desperate attempt to stop
the infection from spreading to other sites

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:36.620
or even into the civilian world, a research
assistant made the choice to detonate the

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.740
on-site nuclear warhead.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:43.960
The infection was stopped, but all remaining
surviving personnel were killed in the blast,

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:48.130
and the surrounding area - afflicted with
irreparable damage.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:53.550
SCP-1100 was moved to a triple-redundant hermetically
sealed container, stored in a containment

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.360
chamber at an unlisted Foundation site.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:00.420
The container is checked daily, to ensure
that it is still completely intact and able

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.270
to hold the substance.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:07.720
If anything should happen to the container,
SCP-1100 is to be immediately transferred

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.150
to a new one.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:14.950
After the devastating loss of Site 26, and
additional experimentation, SCP-1100’s class

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:17.490
was changed from Euclid to Keter.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:22.300
This allowed the Foundation to allocate additional
resources to its containment, seeing as Safe

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:27.620
and Euclid containment procedures had both
resulted in catastrophic loss of human life.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:33.280
And in both instances, they had been profoundly
lucky that it hadn’t been worse.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:37.950
After determining that exposure to SCP-1100
would make edible plants unfit for consumption

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:43.210
and heighten the danger of other normally
innocuous plants, the Foundation became curious

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:47.090
about the effects the substance might have
on animal test subjects.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:52.180
A variety of species were selected for the
animal trials, including deer, mice, cows,

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:54.460
chickens, cats, and dogs.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:59.430
The deer and the mice, both ordinarily considered
to be docile prey animals in the wild, were

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:02.570
the first to be exposed to SCP-1100.

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:06.490
Within 24 hours, they had become much stronger
and more aggressive.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:10.210
One of the deer was able to break down the
door of an observation room by ramming against

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:11.660
it with its head.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:16.460
Once it had broken out of the room, it proceeded
to charge and attack any person that it saw.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:20.971
The mice became prone to swarming researchers
and biting them wherever they could, with

00:07:20.971 --> 00:07:26.030
jaw strength capable of biting through hazmat
suits and even biting one person’s finger

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:27.380
clean off.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:31.540
Any attempts to subdue the animals were futile,
the creatures somehow fighting off even the

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:33.050
strongest sedative.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:37.870
The only way to prevent the infected deer
and mice from continuing to attack was to

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:39.000
terminate them.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.730
Next, the cows and chickens were exposed to
SCP-1100.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:47.590
They did not display any behavioral changes
once exposed, nor did they show any increased

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:48.590
strength.

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:52.630
The cows and chickens continued to behave
normally, going about their days as if nothing

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:53.850
had changed.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:58.010
They did not respond to the presence of humans
with the exception of feeding times, during

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.570
which they would approach only to eat their
food.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:04.620
A selection of the livestock were slaughtered,
in order to perform an autopsy and look for

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.890
anomalies in their bodies.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:10.660
Everything looked unchanged, until some of
the meat was prepared for consumption and

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:13.379
given to a selection of D-class personnel.

00:08:13.379 --> 00:08:17.990
The beef taken from the infected cows was
impossible to digest, causing a dramatic amount

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:21.020
of gastric upset, cramping, and vomiting.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:25.510
Testing showed that, inexplicably, it had
no identifiable nutritional value.

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:30.120
The chicken, on the other hand, became highly
toxic, showing lethal levels of cyanide and

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:33.479
arsenic naturally present in its flesh when
tested.

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:38.860
Like with the fruits and vegetables, exposure
to SCP-1100 made the cows and chickens impossible

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:40.849
for human beings to eat.

00:08:40.849 --> 00:08:43.629
The cats and dogs were last to be experimented
on.

00:08:43.629 --> 00:08:48.870
No matter how docile and friendly the animals
were at first, within 24 hours they had become

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:49.870
vicious.

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:53.720
At the sight of any human, they would attempt
to attack.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:57.860
Like the deer and mice, they could not be
subdued by any level of sedative, displaying

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:01.440
shocking levels of strength and resilience
for their size.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:05.379
One D-Class lost his arm, and another had
his eyes clawed out before the subjects could

00:09:05.379 --> 00:09:06.610
be terminated.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:12.480
Whatever SCP-1100 was, it made everything
it touched dangerous to humans.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:17.870
Even man’s best friend could be convinced
to turn on him in only a single day.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:22.180
As might be expected, given the significant
loss of life and the destruction of two different

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:28.100
Foundation sites, experimentation with SCP-1100
has been suspended until further notice.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:33.620
The substance went from affecting plants and
animals within 72 hours to accomplishing it

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:36.499
in 48, and then 24.

00:09:36.499 --> 00:09:39.779
It is becoming more efficient, and more dangerous.

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:44.579
If allowed to continue adapting, it could
someday transform infected organisms in only

00:09:44.579 --> 00:09:45.839
a minute.

00:09:45.839 --> 00:09:50.139
If the substance ever escapes containment
again, defoliants and desiccants are to be

00:09:50.139 --> 00:09:55.009
deployed within a 1-kilometer radius of the
infected area, and the area must be quarantined

00:09:55.009 --> 00:09:56.670
for 12 months.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:10:01.250
If the situation becomes dire enough, nuclear
or chemical weapons may be deployed in order

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:06.079
to distract the public and provide an acceptable
explanation for the quarantine.

00:10:06.079 --> 00:10:09.600
How had things gone so horribly wrong so fast?

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:14.079
Bits of surveillance video were recovered
from the ruins of Site 26, providing a glimpse

00:10:14.079 --> 00:10:17.910
into what exactly happened before the entire
site was destroyed.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:22.920
The footage pieced together is not entirely
conclusive, but here is what we know for sure:

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:27.509
A Foundation researcher referred to as Dr.
V disarmed and shot the armed guard at the

00:10:27.509 --> 00:10:30.390
entrance to SCP-1100’s containment facility.

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:36.009
While he did this, another Foundation researcher
known as Dr. M entered the containment and

00:10:36.009 --> 00:10:38.670
took the sample of SCP-1100 out.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:42.980
The footage cuts out for a while here, but
it becomes clear when the video resumes that

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:48.110
Dr. V and Dr. M dumped part of the sample
into the Site’s water supply, and vaporized

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:50.170
the rest of it into the air.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:54.809
This is believed to be the cause of the mass
contamination that occurred at the site, which

00:10:54.809 --> 00:10:56.930
was previously thought to have been accidental.

00:10:56.930 --> 00:11:03.079
Dr. V and Dr. M were later linked to an environmentalist
organization on the Foundation’s watch list.

00:11:03.079 --> 00:11:09.040
During the investigation of Dr. V and Dr.
M, a diary was recovered from Dr. V’s home.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:13.589
In it, he wrote about his personal theories
regarding SCP-1100 and where it might have

00:11:13.589 --> 00:11:14.589
come from.

00:11:14.589 --> 00:11:19.560
While his colleagues proposed SCP-1100 was
some sort of deliberately engineered bioweapon,

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:23.860
Dr. V believed it to have a far more organic
point of origin.

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:28.320
He stated plainly: “It’s a planetary immune
response.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:32.639
It’s Gaia, Mother Earth, fighting back against
us.

00:11:32.639 --> 00:11:35.290
The more we try to fight it, the worse it
gets.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:40.089
She wants us all dead, wants us gone because
of what we’ve done to Her.

00:11:40.089 --> 00:11:42.430
And there’s nothing we can do to stop it.”

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:46.380
He concluded the entry with the assertion
that the only thing humanity can do now is

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:49.740
accept the punishment the Earth wishes to
give us.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:55.019
This was his final entry before he and Dr.
M triggered the destruction of Site 26.

00:11:55.019 --> 00:11:56.380
Were the Doctors right?

00:11:56.380 --> 00:12:00.800
Should we just accept that the Earth is done
with humanity, and ready to drive us to extinction

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:03.399
before we can do any further damage?

00:12:03.399 --> 00:12:05.110
The jury’s still out on that.

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:10.189
Perhaps we can turn back the clock, mitigate
the harm done to the natural world, and attempt

00:12:10.189 --> 00:12:13.699
to earn back its favor before it’s too late.

00:12:13.699 --> 00:12:19.290
But if SCP-1100 ever makes its way out of
containment and reaches the plants and animals

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:25.779
of our world, turning them all against us
one by one, we won’t have much of a choice.

00:12:25.779 --> 00:12:31.089
Now go check out “SCP XK Class End of the
World Scenarios Explained” and “SCP-2000

00:12:31.089 --> 00:12:36.329
- Deus Ex Machina” for more SCPs that could
cause or prevent the end of the world as we

00:12:36.329 --> 00:12:36.620
know it!

